Description: no default key bindings when rc.xml has none
 labwc 0.9.3 loads its built-in key bindings (A-Tab, A-S-Tab, A-F4,
 A-Space, W-Return, W-a, W-arrows and the XF86 volume and brightness keys)
 whenever rc.xml defines no keybind, and logs "load default key bindings".
 ThinFloe's rc.xml has a <keyboard> section with no keybind on purpose,
 so the image got the defaults after all: Alt-Tab switched windows on the
 ThinFloe desktop, the tile menu included, instead of reaching the
 ThinLinc session, even when that session was fullscreen.
 .
 post_processing() no longer falls back to the default key bindings. An
 explicit <keyboard><default /> still loads them, and the fallback to the
 default mouse bindings is unchanged.
 .
 thinfloe-specific: not proposed for upstream inclusion, see Forwarded below.
Author: ThinFloe maintainers
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-18
---
--- a/src/config/rcxml.c
+++ b/src/config/rcxml.c
@@ -1680,10 +1680,11 @@
 static void
 post_processing(void)
 {
-	if (!wl_list_length(&rc.keybinds)) {
-		wlr_log(WLR_INFO, "load default key bindings");
-		load_default_key_bindings();
-	}
+	/*
+	 * thinfloe: no fallback to the default key bindings. An rc.xml
+	 * without keybinds means no keybinds; <keyboard><default /> still
+	 * loads them on request.
+	 */
 
 	if (!wl_list_length(&rc.mousebinds)) {
 		wlr_log(WLR_INFO, "load default mouse bindings");
